 when you  don't have a body no question about it  and we had this case it's reminiscent of  jennifer doulos and fotus dulos who  ended up killing himself before there  was any chance of finding the body or  finding out if he was guilty but we do  know that there was strife in the  marriage in both cases that draws a  parallel somebody who was threatening to  leave somebody else and somebody who  didn't want to let go of that individual  so this is a very similar case but i do  believe they did a great job in the  forensic telephones records and actually  getting video footage of him doing those  five separate uh garbage  dumps in that case and it was the same  thing with jennifer and photos doulos  yeah and also that whole dr jekyll and  hyde situation where they were talking  about men who have almost like split  personalities when it comes to dealing  with their wives there's another  similarity thank you both when we come  back inside the tennessee courtroom  where a man convicted of shooting and  killing a deputy is asking a jury to  spare him from the death penalty the  testimony after the break  welcome back a tennessee jury is  continuing to hear evidence in the  penalty phase for a man convicted of  killing a cop now facing either life in  prison or the death penalty  stephen wiggins was found guilty of  fatally shooting dickinson sergeant  daniel baker and lighting baker's body  on fire wiggins stole baker's patrol  vehicle pretended to be baker over the  radio and said he shot baker point blank  because quote it's like a dog you don't  let it suffer defense attorneys say  wiggins has brain damage from being  beaten as a young child which doesn't  excuse his actions but should be  considered as a possible reason to vote  against execution  mr wiggins suffers from a neurocognitive  disorder brain damage  likely he was born this way and has  resulted in seizures hallucinations  reduced ability to reach social cues  irritability impulsivity and emotional  dysregulation  kind of in a nutshell those are the ways  in which his various brain areas have  impacted him  while brain damage is not curable  symptoms like this are treatable  he is being treated with medications  that he was not taking on the street  because he couldn't afford it  as well as he's in a structured  environment and he's done very well and  so it's showing in fact that he can have  a good response with medication and  being in a structured environment uh and  and so there is treatment available  there's good treatment available and  he's responding to it  wiggins declined to take the stand in  his own defense but the defense did call  his mother and brother to talk about  abuse wigan suffered at the hands of his  father including being beat with a  rotary phone  like most other  things it was an object  for him to use  to hit us  if he was  incredibly angry at the time he could  hit stephen anywhere but  every day all day he would hit stephen  in the head  and  would he just pop him in the head or  would he hit him with enough  with some force  it varied  sometimes it was just a pop and  sometimes it was a full  force  i remembered him  dragging me by my hair  all the way out of the house across the  porch  and down the steps  as the boys got older  did did scott's physical abuse of them  increase  i don't know if his  mental  problems got worse  or if he just began to enjoy it more  it just seemed to get worse and worse  and worse to the point that  anything was a weapon  there was weapons knives he's held guns  to her head  lisa the last person executed in  tennessee was in 2018 and he got the  electric chair not after a triple murder  but after he killed another person in  jail so do you think the death sentence  may be too hard for the prosecution to  get in this state  i'm not so sure in this particular case  because it's going to be based on who  makes up the jury and because it needs  to be unanimous you're going to be  looking at people's vario